  "worked_solution": "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)\u2248f(a,b)+\u2207f(a,b)\\cdot \u27e8x-a,y-b\u27e9.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,8)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & \u2248f(2,8)+\u2207f(2,8)\\cdot \u27e8x-2,y-8\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(2,8)=8.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, &  & \u21d2\\, & {f}_{x}(2,8)=\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 8}}=2, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{xy}} &  & \u21d2\\, & {f}_{y}(2,8)=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 8}}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(2,8)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207f(2,8) & =\u27e82,\\frac{1}{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & \u2248f(2,8)+\u2207\\,f(2,8)\\cdot \u27e8x-2,\\,y-8\u27e9 \\\\  & =8+\u27e82,\\frac{1}{2}\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8x-2,\\,y-8\u27e9 \\\\  & =8+2(x-2)+\\frac{1}{2}(y-8) \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{y}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
